Chapter: CpuInspectTest
  cites Dev chapter CpuInspector
  cites Dev chapter HexFormat

 The CPU inspector against the processor this test is running on.

 NO REGISTER VALUE IS ASSERTED, and that is forced rather than chosen. CR3
 is a physical address that moves with the page tables, the vendor string
 differs between hosts, and the feature list differs between a laptop and
 a hypervisor. An expected file naming any of them would pin this test to
 one machine and one boot, and would fail on the next one for a reason
 that is not a defect.

 WHAT IS ASSERTED IS WHAT LONG MODE REQUIRES. This code is executing, so
 the processor is in long mode, so PE and PG must be set, LONG-MODE must
 be reported, CR3 must be page-aligned, and the vendor string must be
 twelve characters. Those hold on every machine that can run this test at
 all, which is exactly the property an expected file needs.

 THE VENDOR LENGTH IS THE CCE CHECK. Twelve bytes go in and twelve
 characters must come out; `from-unicode` returning negative one for a
 byte drops that character, so a broken conversion shortens the string.
 A length of twelve is therefore a statement that all twelve bytes
 converted, without naming a vendor that varies. The three-register order
 is checked the same way -- it cannot be checked by value, but a decode
 reading them in the wrong order still produces twelve characters, so the
 length alone does NOT cover it and this test does not claim to.

 THE OUT-OF-RANGE LEAF REFUSAL IS THE ONE ARM THE MACHINE WILL NOT
 PRODUCE. Every leaf up to the maximum answers something, so the refusal
 is unreachable without asking for a leaf that does not exist; it is
 exercised directly here because an inspector that reported zeroes as a
 real answer is precisely the failure this refusal prevents.

 We say:

Section: Joining

  joined : List Text, Integer, Text -> Text
  joined (xs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs then acc
    else if text-length acc == 0 then joined xs (i + 1) (list-at xs i)
    else joined xs (i + 1) (acc & " | " & list-at xs i)

Section: Contains

  has-word : Text, Text -> Boolean
  has-word (hay) (needle) = has-loop hay needle 0 (text-length hay - text-length needle)

  has-loop : Text, Text, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  has-loop (hay) (needle) (i) (last) =
    if i > last then False
    else if substring hay i (text-length needle) == needle then True
    else has-loop hay needle (i + 1) last

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let cr0 = cpu-read-cr0
    in let cr3 = cpu-read-cr3
    in act
      print-line-uni ("cr0-pe: " & bit-flag cr0 0 & " cr0-pg: " & bit-flag cr0 31)
      print-line-uni ("cr0-line-shape: " & show (has-word ci-cr0-line "PE=1") & " " & show (has-word ci-cr0-line "PG=1"))
      print-line-uni ("cr3-page-aligned: " & show (bit-and cr3 4095 == 0))
      print-line-uni ("cr3-line-has-pml4: " & show (has-word ci-cr3-line "PML4"))
      print-line-uni ("cr-report-lines: " & show (list-length ci-cr-report))

      print-line-uni ("vendor-length: " & show (text-length ci-vendor))
      print-line-uni ("max-leaf-at-least-1: " & show (ci-max-leaf >= 1))

      print-line-uni ("leaf0-accepted: " & show (list-length (ci-leaf-report 0)))
      print-line-uni ("leaf0-shape: " & show (has-word (list-at (ci-leaf-report 0) 0) "eax #"))
      print-line-uni ("leaf-negative: " & joined (ci-leaf-report (0 - 1)) 0 "")
      print-line-uni ("leaf-too-high: " & show (list-length (ci-leaf-report 4096)) & " lines, refused: " & show (has-word (list-at (ci-leaf-report 4096) 0) "refused"))

      print-line-uni ("feat-report-lines: " & show (list-length ci-feat-report))
      print-line-uni ("long-mode-reported: " & show (has-word ci-ext-edx "LONG-MODE"))
      print-line-uni ("sse2-reported: " & show (has-word ci-leaf1-edx "SSE2"))
      print-line-uni ("tsc-reported: " & show (has-word ci-leaf1-edx "TSC"))

 An empty register must render as a word, and under codex-vm leaf 1 ECX
 really is zero, so this line exercises the empty arm on the machine the
 battery runs on rather than needing one contrived.

      print-line-uni ("empty-renders-as-word: " & ci-or-none "")
      print-line-uni ("nonempty-passes-through: " & ci-or-none "SSE2")
    end
  end
